From: Colin Whittaker <colin.whittaker@adtran.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: keep the noise average on return

A channel set restarts the noise average of the phy, and the next
update seeds it from a single IPI histogram reading. After an
off-channel visit, such as a scan dwell, the phy returns to the
operating channel, whose channel state still holds the noise floor
from before. Restarting there makes the noise of the operating channel
jump to one reading and settle again over the next updates. If that
reading has no counts, the driver reports no noise until the next
update.

When mt7915 or mt7996 returns to the operating channel, continue the
average from the noise floor that the channel state holds. Every other
channel set still restarts it.
---
 mt7915/main.c |    8 +++++++-
 mt7996/main.c |    8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -772,7 +772,13 @@ int mt7996_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *
 	/* the firmware replaces the thresholds when it sets a channel */
 	if (!mphy->offchannel)
 		mt7996_apply_edcca_limits(phy);
-	phy->noise = 0;
+	/* back on the operating channel, continue its noise average instead
+	 * of starting it again from a single IPI histogram reading
+	 */
+	if (mphy->chandef.chan == mphy->main_chandef.chan && !mphy->offchannel)
+		phy->noise = -mphy->chan_state->noise << 4;
+	else
+		phy->noise = 0;
 	/* a channel switch of a CSA also lands here, and a beacon upload at
 	 * that point would start a second CSA countdown on the new channel
 	 */
--- a/mt7915/main.c
+++ b/mt7915/main.c
@@ -383,7 +383,13 @@ int mt7915_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *
 	mt7915_mac_cca_stats_reset(phy);
 
 	mt7915_mac_reset_counters(phy);
-	phy->noise = 0;
+	/* back on the operating channel, continue its noise average instead
+	 * of starting it again from a single IPI histogram reading
+	 */
+	if (mphy->chandef.chan == mphy->main_chandef.chan && !mphy->offchannel)
+		phy->noise = -mphy->chan_state->noise << 4;
+	else
+		phy->noise = 0;
 
 out:
 	if (!mt76_testmode_enabled(phy->mt76))
